      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's certainly an interesting observation, and while there is no well-supported scientific evidence that emotions cause physical changes like flickering lights or monitor glitches, stress and emotions undeniably affect your body. It's possible that the stress is causing your hand movements to make subtle changes in your environment, or there could be an underlying technical issue at your workplace that coincidentally aligns with your emotional states. Have you considered taking these occurrences to your IT department to rule out any potential hardware issues? This could help alleviate some of your stress by putting your mind at ease.",
