      "content": "Your experience does sound very specific, and while it's fun to consider the idea of emotional frequencies interacting with an electrical field, there isn't any scientific research supporting this claim. However, it's important to remember that our bodies are highly complex and stress can manifest in various physical ways. Perhaps your heightened emotions are making your body more sensitive to the environment. To further ease any concern, it could be reassuring to monitor your workspace for a longer period under different emotional conditions to look for a pattern more accurately. In the meantime, continue to communicate with IT to ensure there are no overlooked issues, and consider seeking support from a workplace wellness program to learn more strategies for managing stress and frustration.",
